course: dictionary
lesson: 1589
title: Cheap: price, quality and fair
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Cheap has three meanings, so read the sentence to find the right one. Most often it means something costs only a little money. «The biggest pack is often cheaper per unit, but not always, so always do the sum.» Here cheaper is about price: each one costs less.
explain: Cheap can also mean badly made, not worth much even if the price was low. «A cheap toy that broke» tells you the toy was made poorly. Look at the words around it: did it break, was it strong, was the price low?
explain: Cheap can mean not kind or not fair, as in «a cheap trick». Then the word is about how someone behaves, not about money. Ask yourself: is this about money, quality or behaviour? The sentence will tell you.
fact: Cheap means it costs only a little money.
fact: «Cheaper» compares two prices, and «cheapest» picks the lowest price of all.
fact: «Cheaply» is the adverb: you can buy something cheaply.
fact: Cheap can also mean low quality, or not kind and fair, as in «a cheap trick».
fact: The cheapest item is not always the best value, because it may break quickly.
exercise: «The biggest pack is often cheaper per unit, but not always, so always do the sum.» What does cheaper mean here? | *It costs less money | It is kinder to the shopkeeper | It lasts longer | It is bigger and heavier
exercise: «A cheap toy that broke» tells you what cheap suggests about the toy. | Huge and heavy | Made of solid gold | Very expensive and shiny | *Badly made and not strong
exercise: «The shop had the cheapest bikes in town.» What does cheapest pick out? | The biggest bike | The newest bike | *The lowest price | The highest price
test: «He told a cheap trick to win the game.» What does cheap mean here? | Very quick | Costs very little money | *Not kind or fair | Badly made
test: Mia bought the apples ___ at the market, paying less than anyone else. Which word fits the gap? | cheapest | cheaper | *cheaply | cheap
exam: Jayden says «cheap» always means a good deal. Is he right? | Yes, because cheap means kind | *No, cheap can mean poor quality, and a cheap buy may not be good value | No, cheap means expensive | Yes, cheap things are always the best buy
